{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Second independent victim of the same missing-.git mechanism, observed on the same live server:\n\n    reconcile {\"mode\": \"dry-run\"}\n      -> {\"error\": \"command_failed\",\n          \"message\": \"reconcile (dry-run) failed (exit 1): ERROR: reconciler process failed\n           before finalization: Command '['git', '-C', '/app', 'hash-object', '-w',\n           '--stdin']' returned non-zero exit status 128.\"}\n\nreconcile dry-run is documented as non-mutating and always available, and it fails for the same\nreason as review_plan/verify_completion: /app has no git object DB, so \nexits 128. This widens the blast radius beyond the LLM gates and is covered by AC4 (a real git\nobject DB at the repo root) and AC5 (a deploy-time health check)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787815565502359559,"uuid":"8540459e-21dd-4d3a-a340-e507fbcff96d"}